1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Last time on Zombieland Saga, we got a dance lesson from some cool old people.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
But then some scary biker girls had us dancing between a rock and a hard place!

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Guess I just look like an easy target!

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
And get this, their boss turned out to be the daughter of Saki's old ride-or-die gal pal!

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Then our fearless leader cranked up a bike for the world's deadliest game of chicken!

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Thanks to that, we've got some scrappy new fans!

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Glad to have you guys!

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Sweet, we did it! That was killer! I can already see us taking over!

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Don't get carried away! I mean, I'm just saying!

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Saki seems really happy now that one of her old buddies is a fan of ours!

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
And Lily's been bursting with energy ever since her dad started coming to see our performances!

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
I and Junko have been a lot more relaxed since everything that happened with the Saga Rock Festival this summer.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
And me? I still don't have my memories back.

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
I wonder what happened in my life before I died.

15
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:48,799
Huh? A show for 500 people?

16
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:51,519
That's right. You've come very far.

17
00:02:51,579 --> 00:02:53,319
Is that, like, a lot?

18
00:02:53,419 --> 00:02:56,779
Duh! I mean, think. 100 times 5.

19
00:02:56,999 --> 00:02:58,959
Well, we are at that point.

20
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:02,639
This'll be a first for you. You all are the main event.

21
00:03:03,179 --> 00:03:05,299
Can you fill 500 seats on your own?

22
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:07,219
Well, can you, Sakura?

23
00:03:08,299 --> 00:03:09,219
You'd better!

24
00:03:10,219 --> 00:03:11,219
Anyway!

25
00:03:11,219 --> 00:03:14,879
Anyway! You're booked at an exhibition hall in Karatsu.

26
00:03:16,199 --> 00:03:19,059
The famous Furosato Hall Arpino!

27
00:03:22,339 --> 00:03:24,519
Ar... Pino?

28
00:03:24,839 --> 00:03:26,019
Where's that?

29
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,179
Glad you asked.

30
00:03:28,119 --> 00:03:29,679
It's right here!

31
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:36,079
It's cute!

32
00:03:36,079 --> 00:03:36,239
It's cute!

33
00:03:36,239 --> 00:03:41,959
It feels like we're finally staking our claim in this world.

34
00:03:42,699 --> 00:03:45,799
This'll be different than performing under an open sky.

35
00:03:46,039 --> 00:03:46,899
Takes me back.

36
00:03:47,859 --> 00:03:51,119
This is the place where my old group did our very first show in Saga.

37
00:03:51,119 --> 00:03:58,379
Actually, it feels kind of familiar to me, too.

38
00:03:59,459 --> 00:04:01,499
Maybe... I've been here.

39
00:04:02,039 --> 00:04:06,379
Recently, this multi-purpose hall hasn't hosted many musical events.

40
00:04:07,219 --> 00:04:10,859
But after we perform here, perceptions will change.

41
00:04:11,239 --> 00:04:13,939
Thanks to you, Arpino will be recognized as a venue.

42
00:04:13,939 --> 00:04:17,979
And you'll have completed your first step to saving Saga Prefector!

43
00:04:22,659 --> 00:04:23,939
That feeling...

44
00:04:24,939 --> 00:04:29,559
For some reason, I'm super excited now.

45
00:04:29,939 --> 00:04:33,079
Maybe there's something about that place that has to do with my old life.

46
00:04:33,419 --> 00:04:36,579
And when we perform there, I bet the memories will come rushing back.

47
00:04:37,019 --> 00:04:38,119
I can't fall asleep.

48
00:04:38,519 --> 00:04:40,139
I might as well get in some practice instead.

49
00:04:40,139 --> 00:04:41,139
Sakura!

50
00:04:45,139 --> 00:04:45,619
Sakura!

51
00:04:46,819 --> 00:04:47,259
Sakura!

52
00:04:47,939 --> 00:04:48,219
Huh?

53
00:04:48,619 --> 00:04:49,059
Yeah?

54
00:04:50,199 --> 00:04:51,799
You're getting too far ahead.

55
00:04:52,079 --> 00:04:53,699
Try to keep pace with us.

56
00:04:54,219 --> 00:04:55,199
Oh, I'm sorry.

57
00:04:55,999 --> 00:04:57,379
Think you might need a break?

58
00:04:57,959 --> 00:04:59,279
Of course I don't need a break.

59
00:04:59,379 --> 00:05:01,279
I feel like I could keep practicing forever.

60
00:05:01,819 --> 00:05:03,539
This is our big solo show.

61
00:05:03,799 --> 00:05:05,859
We gotta make sure it's perfect, you know?

62
00:05:06,019 --> 00:05:08,459
Damn, you're acting like a bigger nerd than usual.

63
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:09,719
Don't be silly.

64
00:05:10,259 --> 00:05:13,619
Oh, and by the way, I had an idea while I was up all night rehearsing.

65
00:05:13,899 --> 00:05:17,479
I was thinking during the hook it might be cool to throw in an extra step.

66
00:05:17,779 --> 00:05:20,079
Shouldn't we focus on learning the basic pattern?

67
00:05:20,299 --> 00:05:22,799
I get where you're coming from, but just let me show you real quick.

68
00:05:22,919 --> 00:05:24,419
I promise you're gonna love it.

69
00:05:25,559 --> 00:05:26,579
I'm not so sure.

70
00:05:26,919 --> 00:05:27,719
Oh, wait.

71
00:05:27,819 --> 00:05:29,939
The weather is really beautiful today.

72
00:05:30,119 --> 00:05:32,659
It might be fun to practice outside for a change.

73
00:05:33,059 --> 00:05:34,399
Let's go to the roof.

74
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:35,699
We can't do that.

75
00:05:35,899 --> 00:05:37,339
There's no roof access.

76
00:05:37,339 --> 00:05:42,179
Good morning, Fransu Sudolay.

77
00:05:42,239 --> 00:05:43,019
Yee-haw.

78
00:05:43,979 --> 00:05:45,919
Well, straight to business then.

79
00:05:46,339 --> 00:05:50,579
In light of your big concert, you get a special training regimen.

80
00:05:50,899 --> 00:05:52,459
What is that supposed to mean?

81
00:05:52,459 --> 00:05:54,919
You're going to the mountains!

82
00:05:56,219 --> 00:05:57,979
Uh, you can't be serious.

83
00:05:58,159 --> 00:05:58,599
Like, now?

84
00:05:58,679 --> 00:06:00,039
It has to be now!

85
00:06:00,379 --> 00:06:03,919
You can't pull off something like this without a full-on mountain training montage!

86
00:06:04,519 --> 00:06:04,959
See?

87
00:06:04,959 --> 00:06:08,859
You get your butts kicked, you grow, and you return!

88
00:06:09,379 --> 00:06:09,719
Hmm?

89
00:06:10,259 --> 00:06:12,799
And you'll be stuck there till I come to the rescue to live!

90
00:06:12,799 --> 00:06:13,799
Yee-haw!

91
00:06:13,799 --> 00:06:22,899
Do you think there's any real benefit to this?

92
00:06:23,719 --> 00:06:24,799
Hell if I know.

93
00:06:24,939 --> 00:06:28,299
But if he's messing with us, I'm gonna punch the shades right off his face!

94
00:06:29,979 --> 00:06:31,319
Looks like we're here.

95
00:06:32,119 --> 00:06:32,539
Goodness.

96
00:06:33,219 --> 00:06:35,459
He certainly chose a barren spot, didn't he?

97
00:06:35,459 --> 00:06:39,339
If I weren't dead, I'd probably die here.

98
00:06:39,539 --> 00:06:41,919
I feel like a zombie popsicle!

99
00:06:42,259 --> 00:06:43,319
This really sucks.

100
00:06:43,519 --> 00:06:44,159
I'm bored.

101
00:06:44,659 --> 00:06:45,719
What do we do?

102
00:06:46,259 --> 00:06:48,279
We can't practice in a place like this.

103
00:06:51,519 --> 00:06:54,279
If we're dead, can we still freeze to death?

104
00:06:54,419 --> 00:06:55,319
Not to death.

105
00:06:55,499 --> 00:06:57,099
We'd be fine after we thawed out.

106
00:06:57,679 --> 00:06:59,179
Assuming we didn't get eaten.

107
00:06:59,779 --> 00:07:00,119
What?

108
00:07:00,339 --> 00:07:00,619
Eaten?

109
00:07:01,019 --> 00:07:02,459
None of us can freeze!

110
00:07:02,659 --> 00:07:03,339
No one!

111
00:07:03,759 --> 00:07:05,299
It's kind of late for that.

112
00:07:05,459 --> 00:07:05,879
Look.

113
00:07:06,319 --> 00:07:06,719
Tai!

114
00:07:07,579 --> 00:07:09,019
Sure wish we had a fire.

115
00:07:09,479 --> 00:07:11,179
Oh, I can make one for us?

116
00:07:11,279 --> 00:07:11,759
For real?

117
00:07:11,879 --> 00:07:12,619
Sure I can!

118
00:07:12,739 --> 00:07:13,019
Duh!

119
00:07:13,219 --> 00:07:17,019
I mean, I was the lovable star of Girl Scout Mania Case Files 3, remember?

120
00:07:17,499 --> 00:07:18,119
What's that?

121
00:07:18,739 --> 00:07:22,479
In the meantime, I suppose I should try to find something for us to eat.

122
00:07:22,939 --> 00:07:23,599
You're right.

123
00:07:23,859 --> 00:07:26,239
We won't get anything done if we're just sitting around.

124
00:07:26,699 --> 00:07:27,079
Yeah.

125
00:07:27,619 --> 00:07:28,219
But wait.

126
00:07:28,859 --> 00:07:30,059
Shouldn't we be practicing?

127
00:07:30,059 --> 00:07:32,299
We have a autopino coming up.

128
00:07:32,299 --> 00:07:36,239
Yeah, but figuring out how to survive is more important.

129
00:07:36,859 --> 00:07:38,559
Survive is a strong word.

130
00:07:38,879 --> 00:07:41,939
I'm gonna go pick up some branches and stuff we can use as firewood.

131
00:07:42,519 --> 00:07:44,859
Branches from pine trees are really good for that.

132
00:07:45,179 --> 00:07:45,899
Now, now.

133
00:07:46,359 --> 00:07:47,479
Let's get settled.

134
00:07:47,859 --> 00:07:50,119
Then perhaps we can practice a bit.

135
00:07:50,119 --> 00:07:51,059
Okay.

136
00:07:56,579 --> 00:07:57,799
Check it out, squirt.

137
00:07:58,099 --> 00:08:00,759
Here's more sticks than you can shake a stick at.

138
00:08:01,019 --> 00:08:01,919
This is plenty, right?

139
00:08:02,579 --> 00:08:04,019
Hey, don't do that!

140
00:08:04,199 --> 00:08:07,259
I told you, you're supposed to let them dry out by the fire first.

141
00:08:07,679 --> 00:08:07,999
Oops.

142
00:08:08,259 --> 00:08:09,459
Look what I found.

143
00:08:09,819 --> 00:08:11,799
These mushrooms look delightfully tasty.

144
00:08:12,219 --> 00:08:13,199
Though they might be poisonous.

145
00:08:14,039 --> 00:08:14,899
Who cares?

146
00:08:14,899 --> 00:08:15,979
We're zombies!

147
00:08:15,979 --> 00:08:22,819
Stop!

148
00:08:22,979 --> 00:08:25,819
What are you doing?

149
00:08:26,159 --> 00:08:27,699
I'm hunting, obviously.

150
00:08:28,179 --> 00:08:28,599
Hunting?

151
00:08:28,879 --> 00:08:29,179
Shh!

152
00:08:29,339 --> 00:08:30,359
It's under that tree.

153
00:08:33,999 --> 00:08:35,999
Please don't shoot the cute little piggy!

154
00:08:38,139 --> 00:08:38,739
Sorry.

155
00:08:39,379 --> 00:08:40,659
It's no big deal.

156
00:08:40,659 --> 00:08:42,859
I've got a quicker ride than the others.

157
00:08:43,179 --> 00:08:44,739
I'll find something else.

158
00:08:44,739 --> 00:08:46,299
If you say so.

159
00:08:46,959 --> 00:08:48,779
I'm gonna go take a look over there.

160
00:08:49,139 --> 00:08:49,499
You in?

161
00:08:50,199 --> 00:08:50,839
Uh, no.

162
00:08:51,619 --> 00:08:52,579
Think I'll pass.

163
00:09:00,799 --> 00:09:01,319
Sakura.

164
00:09:02,079 --> 00:09:04,079
Are you trying to catch a fish?

165
00:09:04,279 --> 00:09:04,619
Uh-huh.

166
00:09:05,339 --> 00:09:06,919
I get to sit quietly.

167
00:09:07,479 --> 00:09:09,399
So it's kind of the perfect job for me.

168
00:09:10,119 --> 00:09:10,719
I see.

169
00:09:10,719 --> 00:09:14,119
There's so much chaos.

170
00:09:14,619 --> 00:09:14,879
Huh?

171
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:15,579
Really?

172
00:09:15,739 --> 00:09:15,959
Where?

173
00:09:16,679 --> 00:09:18,759
Oh, it's inside your heart, of course.

174
00:09:18,999 --> 00:09:19,399
Oh.

175
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,819
Is there something bothering you?

176
00:09:22,599 --> 00:09:23,759
Well, yeah.

177
00:09:24,659 --> 00:09:27,899
I guess I just want to feel like all of us are doing the best we can.

178
00:09:28,279 --> 00:09:32,399
And I think we need to practice a lot more if we want the concert to be any good.

179
00:09:32,399 --> 00:09:33,479
I know you do.

180
00:09:34,219 --> 00:09:35,779
But panicking won't help.

181
00:09:36,319 --> 00:09:38,819
It's like when you're fishing and don't catch anything.

182
00:09:40,119 --> 00:09:42,079
You wonder how deep the fish are.

183
00:09:42,919 --> 00:09:44,279
Did you use the right bait?

184
00:09:44,919 --> 00:09:46,719
Or maybe you picked a bad spot.

185
00:09:47,539 --> 00:09:50,219
If you're calm and think about it from different angles,

186
00:09:50,839 --> 00:09:52,879
you can usually find the answer, you know?

187
00:09:52,879 --> 00:09:58,419
We did it!

188
00:10:01,919 --> 00:10:04,919
I have to make sure I'm ready to perform at Arpino.

189
00:10:06,059 --> 00:10:07,679
Even if I'm all alone.

190
00:10:11,379 --> 00:10:14,599
We've been here a few days and nobody's gotten eaten yet,

191
00:10:14,719 --> 00:10:16,179
so I'd say we're killing it.

192
00:10:16,639 --> 00:10:20,299
But still, we've got one thing left that needs to be done.

193
00:10:20,599 --> 00:10:22,339
Something that's really important.

194
00:10:22,339 --> 00:10:23,659
I'm so glad!

195
00:10:24,099 --> 00:10:24,799
Thank you!

196
00:10:25,159 --> 00:10:26,779
I thought you guys had forgotten it.

197
00:10:26,919 --> 00:10:27,439
No way!

198
00:10:28,279 --> 00:10:29,359
We need meat!

199
00:10:29,859 --> 00:10:31,679
And not just fish, either.

200
00:10:31,939 --> 00:10:32,719
We're zombies.

201
00:10:32,879 --> 00:10:34,559
We gotta have something worth catching.

202
00:10:34,999 --> 00:10:38,599
I've been trying my best, but that baby boar is just so skittish.

203
00:10:38,819 --> 00:10:40,759
Don't beat yourself up about it.

204
00:10:40,919 --> 00:10:42,239
We're new to this.

205
00:10:42,699 --> 00:10:45,239
None of us really know how to mess with wild game.

206
00:10:46,259 --> 00:10:48,399
All right, let's talk about who does what.

207
00:10:48,779 --> 00:10:49,959
Sure, sounds good.

208
00:10:50,019 --> 00:10:50,419
Okay!

209
00:10:52,339 --> 00:10:57,319
The trap's totally hidden.

210
00:10:57,839 --> 00:10:58,279
Good.

211
00:10:58,719 --> 00:11:00,579
He'll come by any minute now.

212
00:11:00,899 --> 00:11:02,339
Are you sure about this?

213
00:11:03,899 --> 00:11:04,919
He's close.

214
00:11:05,879 --> 00:11:06,939
Okay, hide!

215
00:11:07,659 --> 00:11:09,059
Hey, wait up!

216
00:11:09,059 --> 00:11:13,119
Oh my word.

217
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:15,079
She just ruined the trap!

218
00:11:15,139 --> 00:11:15,479
Saki!

219
00:11:18,479 --> 00:11:19,879
Okay, don't move!

220
00:11:19,879 --> 00:11:30,099
What the hell is that?

221
00:11:30,539 --> 00:11:32,339
I guess he's the daddy boar!

222
00:11:33,339 --> 00:11:34,519
One thing's clear.

223
00:11:34,799 --> 00:11:36,479
We need a much bigger pit.

224
00:11:36,479 --> 00:11:39,159
Oh no, this is about to get worse.

225
00:11:41,979 --> 00:11:42,819
Oh my god!

226
00:11:43,159 --> 00:11:43,699
What do I do?

227
00:11:43,839 --> 00:11:44,359
What do I do?

228
00:11:44,419 --> 00:11:44,939
What do I do?

229
00:11:44,979 --> 00:11:45,479
What do I do?

230
00:11:45,539 --> 00:11:46,059
What do I do?

231
00:11:46,139 --> 00:11:46,679
What do I do?

232
00:11:47,339 --> 00:11:47,879
What do I do?

233
00:11:47,879 --> 00:11:48,879
This nice piggy!

234
00:11:49,099 --> 00:11:49,719
Damn it!

235
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:51,019
How do we save her?

236
00:11:51,819 --> 00:11:53,359
I think I might have an idea.

237
00:11:53,859 --> 00:11:56,739
I learned it from a joy missionary back in Shimabara.

238
00:11:56,739 --> 00:11:58,959
Listen carefully, Lady Sakura.

239
00:11:59,299 --> 00:12:00,539
You need to play dead.

240
00:12:00,859 --> 00:12:02,199
But she is dead.

241
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:03,819
Come on.

242
00:12:09,039 --> 00:12:11,699
He chomped her head!

243
00:12:11,699 --> 00:12:30,859
You okay, Sakura?

244
00:12:31,099 --> 00:12:31,759
Say something!

245
00:12:33,339 --> 00:12:34,699
Is this wrong?

246
00:12:35,279 --> 00:12:36,099
No joke.

247
00:12:36,419 --> 00:12:38,139
That thing was really disgusting.

248
00:12:38,679 --> 00:12:39,699
Not the boar.

249
00:12:39,699 --> 00:12:40,919
I mean this.

250
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:43,579
We're supposed to be running our dance routines,

251
00:12:43,819 --> 00:12:45,639
not running away from wild animals.

252
00:12:46,699 --> 00:12:49,379
We should be showered in spotlights, not drool.

253
00:12:49,779 --> 00:12:51,159
There's not much time left.

254
00:12:51,579 --> 00:12:54,359
So why are we spending it on pointless stuff like this?

255
00:12:54,499 --> 00:12:55,479
Oh, I see now.

256
00:12:56,759 --> 00:12:57,579
Found you!

257
00:12:58,299 --> 00:13:00,399
The good yodel old lady day!

258
00:13:00,539 --> 00:13:01,519
Lady, lady, lady!

259
00:13:02,999 --> 00:13:04,039
How'd it go?

260
00:13:04,239 --> 00:13:07,139
Did you learn any yodel lady, yodel lady, yodel lady life lessons?

261
00:13:07,419 --> 00:13:08,059
Are you kidding?

262
00:13:08,059 --> 00:13:09,159
Just look at us.

263
00:13:09,159 --> 00:13:12,299
Your idiotic games won't prepare us for anything.

264
00:13:12,719 --> 00:13:14,659
The big show is only days away.

265
00:13:14,879 --> 00:13:16,339
I see no point being here.

266
00:13:16,439 --> 00:13:17,279
I'm over it.

267
00:13:17,779 --> 00:13:18,619
Don't you?

268
00:13:19,319 --> 00:13:20,859
Then you should close your eyes.

269
00:13:21,159 --> 00:13:21,679
And listen.

270
00:13:22,359 --> 00:13:24,839
That way, dear Mother Gaia will speak.

271
00:13:25,199 --> 00:13:26,159
And then you'll know!

272
00:13:26,539 --> 00:13:28,899
Even up here, you are never alone!

273
00:13:28,899 --> 00:13:31,219
I just said I've had enough!

274
00:13:31,419 --> 00:13:31,839
Oh, my.

275
00:13:36,519 --> 00:13:37,879
I'm going home!

276
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:38,499
What?

277
00:13:41,139 --> 00:13:42,139
Great job.

278
00:13:42,859 --> 00:13:43,959
So what's the plan?

279
00:13:43,959 --> 00:13:45,959
Go home!

280
00:13:45,959 --> 00:14:08,239
This is bad.

281
00:14:08,239 --> 00:14:11,799
Things have been super awkward since yesterday on the mountain.

282
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:15,539
But our performance at Arpino is right around the corner.

283
00:14:17,099 --> 00:14:17,699
Sakura!

284
00:14:18,059 --> 00:14:20,419
At this rate, we'll be way under-rehearsed.

285
00:14:20,659 --> 00:14:21,179
Sakura!

286
00:14:22,659 --> 00:14:23,999
You're still fast.

287
00:14:24,799 --> 00:14:28,419
Like I said before, you need to match our pace.

288
00:14:29,459 --> 00:14:30,859
This isn't a solo.

289
00:14:32,619 --> 00:14:34,379
Let's try again from the top.

290
00:14:34,379 --> 00:14:36,979
It's not my fault we're out of sync.

291
00:14:39,679 --> 00:14:41,839
Well, you guys were goofing off out there.

292
00:14:42,459 --> 00:14:44,739
I was actually practicing our dance!

293
00:14:49,259 --> 00:14:50,559
Well, that was rude.

294
00:14:50,799 --> 00:14:51,479
What gives?

295
00:15:00,239 --> 00:15:01,359
Welcome to…

296
00:15:01,359 --> 00:15:01,539
Huh?

297
00:15:03,419 --> 00:15:04,019
Greetings.

298
00:15:04,939 --> 00:15:05,499
Gentlemen.

299
00:15:06,559 --> 00:15:07,639
What is it you want?

300
00:15:08,139 --> 00:15:10,959
Well, I am a courtesan.

301
00:15:11,299 --> 00:15:12,599
You're here to dance?

302
00:15:14,179 --> 00:15:16,119
I'm also trained as a geisha.

303
00:15:16,739 --> 00:15:18,059
Not what I asked.

304
00:15:18,799 --> 00:15:20,919
You sent all of us into the mountains,

305
00:15:21,259 --> 00:15:24,659
hoping that Lady Sakura would find some inner peace before the concert.

306
00:15:25,339 --> 00:15:26,099
Is that right?

307
00:15:26,099 --> 00:15:36,059
The beauty of a group is that it makes up for individual weaknesses, resulting in greater collective strength.

308
00:15:36,899 --> 00:15:40,119
But if Sakura can't see that, what's the point?

309
00:15:40,119 --> 00:15:41,379
Indeed, sir.

310
00:15:41,379 --> 00:15:41,879
Indeed, sir.

311
00:15:42,379 --> 00:15:44,119
But couldn't you just tell her?

312
00:15:44,379 --> 00:15:46,519
It's something she needs to learn for herself.

313
00:15:47,799 --> 00:15:49,539
You're different with Lady Sakura.

314
00:15:50,039 --> 00:15:51,519
She must be dear to you.

315
00:15:51,519 --> 00:15:55,279
I only care about saving Saga.

316
00:15:55,279 --> 00:15:59,679
And I have a soft spot for those who can't express themselves.

317
00:15:59,679 --> 00:16:03,859
Saga's depopulation problem is so exhausting.

318
00:16:04,859 --> 00:16:08,399
Every time we climb one mountain, there's a taller one.

319
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:13,979
And now, with this show, it's like we're lost in the wild.

320
00:16:13,979 --> 00:16:16,499
Listen, I'll be honest here.

321
00:16:16,699 --> 00:16:17,779
I think she can do it.

322
00:16:29,039 --> 00:16:31,299
That's enough foolishness, Lord Kotaro.

323
00:16:31,779 --> 00:16:34,879
Mark my words, that brave girl can do anything.

324
00:16:35,819 --> 00:16:37,739
Yeah, that's what I just...

325
00:16:37,739 --> 00:16:39,279
You should have more faith in her.

326
00:16:39,279 --> 00:16:44,439
I just said I do.

327
00:16:45,139 --> 00:16:46,499
You guys heard me, right?

328
00:16:52,019 --> 00:16:54,039
It just keeps getting more complicated.

329
00:16:54,679 --> 00:16:55,919
How can I make this right?

330
00:16:57,299 --> 00:17:00,599
I mean, no matter what, I want the concert to be great.

331
00:17:03,319 --> 00:17:06,359
That venue might have some kind of connection to my past.

332
00:17:06,919 --> 00:17:08,959
And performing there could be huge for us.

333
00:17:09,279 --> 00:17:11,459
We have to do everything we can.

334
00:17:12,959 --> 00:17:13,639
It's okay.

335
00:17:14,039 --> 00:17:15,319
I know I'm in the right here.

336
00:17:15,639 --> 00:17:18,459
And after we put on a good show, I'm sure they'll understand.

337
00:17:20,139 --> 00:17:22,519
So everybody knows their positions now, right?

338
00:17:23,139 --> 00:17:23,579
Yeah!

339
00:17:24,299 --> 00:17:26,459
Alright, let's try the whole thing from the beginning.

340
00:17:30,139 --> 00:17:30,819
It's funny.

341
00:17:30,819 --> 00:17:34,159
I've never actually watched Franshu-shu from the outside.

342
00:17:34,159 --> 00:17:35,159
Let's talk about this part.

343
00:17:35,159 --> 00:17:39,299
It kind of feels like I'm standing in one place for too long.

344
00:17:39,299 --> 00:17:40,299
I see.

345
00:17:40,299 --> 00:17:44,979
Oh, you must mean the bit when we're across from each other.

346
00:17:44,979 --> 00:17:45,979
Yeah, exactly.

347
00:17:45,979 --> 00:17:46,979
Hmm.

348
00:17:46,979 --> 00:17:48,659
Well, Arpino's a pretty big place.

349
00:17:48,659 --> 00:17:51,919
Do you want to try spreading out farther on the sides?

350
00:17:51,919 --> 00:17:52,339
Like, get this part?

351
00:17:52,339 --> 00:17:53,339
Oh, good idea!

352
00:17:53,339 --> 00:17:58,019
The extra space would give me and Junko more room to move, too.

353
00:17:58,019 --> 00:17:59,019
That sounds great.

354
00:17:59,019 --> 00:18:01,019
Hey, if you want me to, I could just switch positions.

355
00:18:01,019 --> 00:18:02,019
Let's talk about this part.

356
00:18:02,019 --> 00:18:03,019
Let's talk about this part.

357
00:18:03,019 --> 00:18:04,019
Kind of feels like I'm standing in one place for too long.

358
00:18:04,019 --> 00:18:05,019
I see.

359
00:18:05,019 --> 00:18:08,019
Oh, you must mean the bit when we're across from each other?

360
00:18:08,019 --> 00:18:09,019
Yeah, exactly.

361
00:18:09,019 --> 00:18:10,019
Hmm.

362
00:18:10,019 --> 00:18:13,019
Well, Arpino's a pretty big place.

363
00:18:13,019 --> 00:18:16,019
Do you want to try spreading out farther on the sides?

364
00:18:16,019 --> 00:18:17,019
Like, get this part?

365
00:18:17,019 --> 00:18:18,019
Oh, good idea!

366
00:18:18,019 --> 00:18:23,019
The extra space would give me and Junko more room to move, too.

367
00:18:23,019 --> 00:18:24,019
That sounds great.

368
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:29,019
Hey, if you want me to, I could just switch positions with Tai.

369
00:18:29,019 --> 00:18:32,019
Oh, I get it.

370
00:18:32,019 --> 00:18:33,019
Everyone moves around Sakura.

371
00:18:33,019 --> 00:18:35,019
That sounds really interesting.

372
00:18:35,019 --> 00:18:36,019
Let's do it!

373
00:18:36,019 --> 00:18:38,019
I love it when a plan comes together.

374
00:18:38,019 --> 00:18:40,019
Let's make sure we've got it down so it'll be easy to...

375
00:18:40,019 --> 00:18:42,019
These guys haven't been rehearsing at all.

376
00:18:42,019 --> 00:18:45,019
So how did they get so in sync?

377
00:18:45,019 --> 00:18:50,019
It must be because they pulled together to make the best of those harsh conditions.

378
00:18:50,019 --> 00:18:53,019
Everyone except me.

379
00:18:55,019 --> 00:18:57,019
You're back!

380
00:18:57,019 --> 00:18:59,019
I'm sorry.

381
00:18:59,019 --> 00:19:03,019
I've been thinking, and I see now that I was being selfish.

382
00:19:03,019 --> 00:19:07,019
Ever since I found out about the Arpino show, I've just been so worked up.

383
00:19:07,019 --> 00:19:11,019
I started obsessing over doing a great job and making everything perfect.

384
00:19:11,019 --> 00:19:15,019
But because of that, I didn't consider you guys.

385
00:19:15,019 --> 00:19:17,019
I forgot about Fran Shushu.

386
00:19:17,019 --> 00:19:19,019
About our team.

387
00:19:19,019 --> 00:19:21,019
Yeah, that explains it.

388
00:19:21,019 --> 00:19:24,019
I thought you seemed kinda hot under the collar.

389
00:19:24,019 --> 00:19:26,019
You still haven't figured it out?

390
00:19:26,019 --> 00:19:28,019
Mr. Kotaro?

391
00:19:28,019 --> 00:19:30,019
Think Niji no Matsubara.

392
00:19:30,019 --> 00:19:32,019
A pine forest.

393
00:19:32,019 --> 00:19:34,019
Pine as in Alpine.

394
00:19:34,019 --> 00:19:36,019
Alpine as in the Alps.

395
00:19:36,019 --> 00:19:38,019
Hence the mountains.

396
00:19:38,019 --> 00:19:40,019
Mountain climbing.

397
00:19:40,019 --> 00:19:42,019
Except with your issues.

398
00:19:42,019 --> 00:19:45,019
I have no idea what that means.

399
00:19:45,019 --> 00:19:47,019
But I'll do my best, sir.

400
00:19:49,019 --> 00:19:51,019
You guys.

401
00:19:54,019 --> 00:19:55,019
Okay!

402
00:19:55,019 --> 00:19:58,019
Let's work hard and make this the best show ever!

403
00:19:58,019 --> 00:19:59,019
Yeah!

404
00:19:59,019 --> 00:20:04,019
I'm glad everything worked out.

405
00:20:04,019 --> 00:20:05,019
What do you mean?

406
00:20:13,019 --> 00:20:14,019
Good morning, Ai!

407
00:20:14,019 --> 00:20:15,019
I'm going running!

408
00:20:15,019 --> 00:20:18,019
Keep an eye out for traffic!

409
00:20:18,019 --> 00:20:19,019
Okay!

410
00:20:19,019 --> 00:20:22,019
There's one week left before our big solo concert.

411
00:20:22,019 --> 00:20:25,019
I've got all the songs and dances memorized.

412
00:20:25,019 --> 00:20:27,019
And we're totally in sync!

413
00:20:27,019 --> 00:20:29,019
So I'm beyond excited!

414
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:31,019
Plus, if I step onto that stage,

415
00:20:31,019 --> 00:20:33,019
maybe I'll remember something important.

416
00:20:33,019 --> 00:20:37,019
And then I'll finally be able to make peace with my past life!

417
00:20:37,019 --> 00:20:40,019
I know my future will be full of happiness and excitement!

418
00:20:40,019 --> 00:20:43,019
Come on, Romero!

419
00:20:43,019 --> 00:20:45,019
Here I go!

420
00:20:45,019 --> 00:20:58,019
Oh, God!

421
00:20:58,019 --> 00:20:59,019
Poor girl!

422
00:20:59,019 --> 00:21:01,019
Let me check!

423
00:21:03,019 --> 00:21:04,019
Go get help!

424
00:21:04,019 --> 00:21:05,019
Okay, doggy?

425
00:21:08,019 --> 00:21:09,019
Be right back!

426
00:21:15,019 --> 00:21:33,019
Where am I?

427
00:21:33,019 --> 00:21:35,019
I don't...

428
00:21:45,019 --> 00:21:46,019
You!

429
00:21:46,019 --> 00:21:47,019
You!

430
00:21:48,019 --> 00:21:49,019
You!

431
00:21:49,019 --> 00:21:50,019
You?!

432
00:21:51,019 --> 00:21:53,019
You!

433
00:21:54,019 --> 00:21:55,019
You!

434
00:21:55,019 --> 00:21:55,999
You!

435
00:23:25,029 --> 00:23:33,389
Lily here? Ron Shushu's really become an unstoppable team! I can't wait to dazzle everyone at the big show!

436
00:23:33,909 --> 00:23:39,409
Next time on Zombieland Saga Episode 11, One-of-a-Kind Saga! Don't miss it!

